            0.121
          ],
          "content": "STATISTICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.863,
            0.104,
            0.898,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "193"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.9,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": "a class interval. It is, therefore, necessary to find the value inside a class that divides the whole distribution into two halves. But which class should this be?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.192,
            0.9,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": "To find this class, we find the cumulative frequencies of all the classes and $\\frac { n } { 2 }$ We now locate the class whose cumulative frequency is greater than (and nearest to) $\\frac { n } { 2 }$ This is called the median class. In the distribution above, $n = 53.\\  So , \\frac{n}{2} = 26.5$ Now 60 – 70 is the class whose cumulative frequency 29 is greater than (and nearest $\\mathrm{t o)} \\frac{n}{2}   , \\mathrm{i.e.}, 26.5.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.367,
            0.487,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, 60 – 70 is the **median class**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.395,
            0.9,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": "After finding the median class, we use the following formula for calculating the median."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.443,
            0.578,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Media} = l + \\left(\\frac{\\frac{n}{2} - \\mathrm{cf}}{f}\\right) \\times h,",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.533,
            0.542,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "where l = lower limit of median class,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.558,
            0.508,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": "n = number of observations,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.583,
            0.833,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": "cf = cumulative frequency of class preceding the median class,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.608,
            0.538,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": "f = frequency of median class,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.634,
            0.692,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": "h = class size (assuming class size to be equal)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.663,
            0.694,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "Substituting the values $\\frac{n}{2}=26.5,\\;l=60,\\;cf=22,\\;f=7,\\;h=10.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.706,
            0.377,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": "in the formula above, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.732,
            0.628,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} \\text{1 }  Mediam  = 60 + \\left( \\frac{26.5 - 22}{7} \\right) \\times 100 \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{4 } \\\\ \\text{5 } \\\\ \\text{6 } \\\\ \\text{6 } \\\\ \\text{7 } \\\\ \\text{8 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{3 } \\\\ \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{1 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\\\ \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 2 } \\text{2 2 2 \\text{2 2 } \\text{2 2 2 } \\text{2 2 2 } \\text{2 